Subject: PCI: dwc: wait longer for the QCA6490 link on the Samsung SM-X710

The X710's WCN6855/QCA6490 is powered by pci-pwrctrl inside the host init
and takes more than the 900 ms dw_pcie_wait_for_link() allows before it is
detected; this kernel never rescans a late link, so the endpoint was only
ever found after a suspend/resume cycle re-ran the wait. Wait 3.6 s on
this board only.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c	2026-11-05 14:34:27.084299547 -0800
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c	2026-11-05 14:34:27.099804720 -0800
@@ -767,17 +767,26 @@
 int dw_pcie_wait_for_link(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 {
 	u32 offset, val, ltssm;
-	int retries;
+	int retries, max_retries = PCIE_LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES;
+
+	/*
+	 * Samsung SM-X710 (gts9wifi): the QCA6490 is powered by pci-pwrctrl
+	 * right before this wait and needs well over a second after WLAN_EN
+	 * before its receivers are detected.  Nothing rescans the bus when the
+	 * link trains late, so give it the time here instead.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9wifi"))
+		max_retries = 4 * PCIE_LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES;
 
 	/* Check if the link is up or not */
-	for (retries = 0; retries < PCIE_LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES; retries++) {
+	for (retries = 0; retries < max_retries; retries++) {
 		if (dw_pcie_link_up(pci))
 			break;
 
 		msleep(PCIE_LINK_WAIT_SLEEP_MS);
 	}
 
-	if (retries >= PCIE_LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES) {
+	if (retries >= max_retries) {
 		/*
 		 * If the link is in Detect.Quiet or Detect.Active state, it
 		 * indicates that no device is detected.
